          "description": "The source names a nominal 95% ethanol preparation. The percentage basis, solvent balance, denaturants and historical product specification are unreported. Different source accessions or receiving stocks prove neither equal nor different supplied preparations. A shared bounded nominal representation is a possible coordinator outcome; exact historical formulation equality and a final owner choice remain unresolved under #1237. This identifier is retained only as a conditional historical proposal handle. Do not install all four candidates as proven distinct substances. Retain all 17 precise occurrence routes and the original source lineages. CHEBI:16236 grounds the named ethanol component only; NCIT:C185110 is not approved because it specifically requires aqueous 95% by volume. No numerical component percentage, water balance or whole-stock molecular identity is inferred. All inherited holds remain. Source-specific context: DSMZ 78 defines vitamin K1 stock with 0.1 ml vitamin K1 and 20 ml nominal 95% ethanol; its vitamin K3 instructions dissolve menadione at 5 mg/ml in that ethanol and then dilute to 0.05 mg/ml with water. DSMZ 104 and 212a explicitly refer to medium 78 for K1. The captured current DSMZ 110 representation links the shared MediaDive K1 solution 125 and K3 solution 5540. Preserve all twelve routed occurrences and distinguish the subsequent K3 water dilution from the unspecified balance of supplied 95% ethanol.",
