      "created_at": "2026-11-08T08:16:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-08T08:16:17Z",
      "body": "Record five additional findings from Worker05's independent review of its unpublished correction draft. These are `W05-FINAL-SKEPTIC-CHEM-001` through `005`. Original findings and failed/intermediate drafts remain evidence; this comment does not claim that every diagnostic report correction was made after GitHub filing. No maintained ingredient change has been applied.\n\n1. **001, bottom-layer explanation:** the primary-conclusions draft incorrectly contrasts FeS with zero-valent iron. JCM629 explicitly reuses JCM628 with artificial saltwater replacing Modified Wolfe mineral solution; both bottom layers retain the FeS preparation and agarose. Correct the report explanation while preserving the already-correct selected payloads. Root verified the complete captured JCM628/629 texts.\n2. **002, MKP attribution:** the primary-conclusions draft calls MKP a JCM salt preparation. The complete MediaDive record identifies DSMZ medium1895 and MKP solution6635, a multicomponent medium base including CMRL1066, Neopeptone, HEPES and glucose. Correct report attribution and scope; the selected payload already cites MediaDive1895.\n3. **003, thiamine-HCl monohydrate completeness:** six NBRC recipes1550/1443/1444/1445/1447/1507 explicitly print the one-water label. Root rehashed and read all six primary captures. Missing CAS, fixed molecular structure or chloride/protonation detail prevents exact molecular grounding; it does not alone rule out a bounded source-defined material under MAPPING_SEMANTICS§3. Reassess one shared nominal monohydrate candidate after ignored-inclusive owner/proposal checks, retaining all six occurrences and both source cases. Do not infer CAS, formula, chloride stoichiometry, supplier, anhydrous/dihydrate equivalence, an exact parent relation, or a separate owner per source number. If an actual owner-boundary ambiguity prevents that representation, document it precisely. The exact successor still requires independent review; this finding is not an identity approval.\n4. **004, reviewer prose count:** the DSMZ95% ethanol grouping has twelve applicable occurrence IDs: eleven flat occurrences plus DSMZ212a. The exact occurrence list was already correct; change the review's “eleven” wording while retaining its predecessor. This supplies no new percentage basis or product-equivalence decision.\n5. **005, reviewer grade wording:** the Tris hydrochloride payload stores `NARROW_MATCH`, and the pinned native projection emits `skos:broadMatch` plus CAS and local identity rows. Two review sentences incorrectly say the stored grade is `BROAD_MATCH`. Correct those sentences; retain the already-correct payload and projection. This is a report correction within the separately filed#1238 decision, not a grade-rule change.\n\nThe bounded source-completion task remains under this issue. Retain each finding's real timestamps, original severity and before/after evidence; do not recast earlier internal report revisions as post-filing repairs. Independently review final selected bytes, complete case/proposal retention and every unchanged scientific hold before publication. Private root readback and complete original findings are in `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/w05-review-followups-triage-v1/`. There is no new role, whole-owner or supported-export approval.\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
